WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.741 --> 00:00:04.408
(pulsing music)

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:07.960
- Well I've always been different,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.940
not wanted to be different.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.140
And just the heels at a very young age

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.653
was just a great statement for it.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.540
I do what I want and (bleep) you.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.868
(laughing)

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.451
(upbeat music)

00:00:26.198 --> 00:00:28.865
(hip hop music)

00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:33.914
♪ Look at all these fools ♪

00:00:33.914 --> 00:00:35.977
♪ They keep trying to be cool ♪

00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:40.730
- I'm Yanis Marshal, I'm a
French Dancer, Choreographer,

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:45.475
and I'm known, I guess, to be
a man that dances in heels.

00:00:45.475 --> 00:00:46.700
(hip hop music continues)

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.884
♪ Now watch me run this ♪

00:00:49.884 --> 00:00:51.813
♪ Look at how I run this ♪

00:00:51.813 --> 00:00:53.610
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah ♪

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.720
Heels is definitely not

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.940
just putting a pair of heels

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.480
and starting to dance with them.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.250
That's not what we're trying to do.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.610
We're trying to really
make it a new style.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.420
Just as you would put it as
hip hop, jazz, and ballet.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.272
♪ Now we got something in common ♪

00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:11.043
I have choreographed a Cirque
du Soleil show, Zumanity.

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.790
I've worked with Celine
Dion and Ryan Reynolds,

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.477
I was playing Deadpool but in heels.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.727
♪ Look at how I run this ♪

00:01:19.727 --> 00:01:21.418
♪ Just run this ♪

00:01:21.418 --> 00:01:22.573
- Thank you so much!

00:01:22.573 --> 00:01:25.224
(crowd applauding and cheering)

00:01:25.224 --> 00:01:28.141
(electronic music)

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.940
- [Yanis] I'm happy when people
tell me that it looks easy

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.480
because it really isn't.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.772
When I dance I always try
to make it look effortless.

00:01:36.772 --> 00:01:39.650
(electronic music continues)

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.660
The risk of dancing in
heels is very simple,

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.593
you can fall at any moment.

00:01:43.593 --> 00:01:44.560
(giggles)

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.393
I think the secret

00:01:45.393 --> 00:01:47.540
is never to forget that
you're wearing heels.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.840
When I teach, I do tell my students

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.180
that it's not enough to be a good dancer.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.760
They have to be stars in their own way.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.873
They have to have, what I
say the most, is charisma.

00:01:59.873 --> 00:02:02.700
(Yanis clicking tongue in time)

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.000
I chose art because, like many
different artists I'm sure,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.540
it was just a way of expressing ourself.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.620
And dance was my way of
screaming, pretty much,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.753
or saying things that I couldn't.

00:02:14.753 --> 00:02:16.600
Now I'm pretty outspoken.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.020
That wasn't always like that.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.173
I think dance helped me become like that.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:24.343
(plane engine roaring)

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.420
(electronic music)

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.660
People would only focus on the heels,

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.080
just the heels, the heels.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.317
And at some point I was like,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.477
"It's not just the shoe itself,

00:02:33.477 --> 00:02:34.970
"It's what it represents."

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.913
It's the fact that men
are not supposed to do it.

00:02:36.913 --> 00:02:37.746
It's the fact that

00:02:37.746 --> 00:02:39.320
if I'm going to walk on
the street with them,

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.746
people will stare.

00:02:40.746 --> 00:02:42.760
(electronic music continues)

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.370
You can't disassociate that

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.200
being gay and dancing in heels as a man.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.033
You can't.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.870
And I think some people have to do it

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.580
so that others can feel
it's okay to do it.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.290
Not just in your room.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.910
I started very young.

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.490
My mother decided to put me up

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.750
in a professional training dance school.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.430
And as I was getting older I
had my sexuality happening,

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.300
and so the heels came with that.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.340
I just think it's a little bit easier,

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.782
for sure, to be gay now.

00:03:07.782 --> 00:03:11.070
Definitely when I was 15 and
where I was from it wasn't.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.520
It was not.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.353
Yeah.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.823
No, no but I was still gay.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.443
Same. (laughs)

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.890
I didn't need heels, trust me.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.042
You knew.

00:03:25.042 --> 00:03:27.959
(electronic music)

00:03:47.973 --> 00:03:50.140
(laughs)

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.090
Right, left, right, left.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.340
I've been told that when I teach a class,

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.690
that I also teach them
a little bit about life.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.880
More than just dance.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.510
Throw in front, woo.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.922
Because I think it goes together.

00:04:01.922 --> 00:04:05.230
You can't be this great, rebel dancer

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.850
if you're not like that in real life.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.820
I am like that.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.433
The way I dance is the way I am.

00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:11.900
Woo! (crowd laughs)

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.720
I don't believe I'm the
first man to dance in heels.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.630
At all.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.324
I think what I've done is
made it very okay to do it.

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:22.810
I'm definitely aware of
the influence that I have.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.473
I only do what I do so
I can inspire people.

